All,

Following is a treatment of "cold fusion".  CMF (Doug Zak) fans fears about=
 cold fusion in concert with their representation of their insurance causin=
g the customer to infer he is protected by CMF from failures that can resul=
t and that they or the product manufacturer will pay the damages for fusion=
 failures.

Comments by Jim Craig (the face of McElroy now retired) on the McElroy Disc=
ussion Forum website.

"A cold fusion is usually a result of heating the pipe under fusion pressur=
e and then applying the fusion pressure.  When the fusion pressure is appli=
ed, most of the molten PE is pushed out of the joint area and the result is=
 a smooth cold interface that usually will not pass a sustained pressure, t=
ensile or bend back test.  This is the result of using an improper fusion p=
rocedure."
The cause of cold fusion being "improper fusion procedure", by definition t=
he contractor must be held accountable.  No manufacturer or manufacturer's =
product liability insurance company will cover a failure that is due to ins=
tallation error and not the result of a product manufacturing defect.  This=
 includes CMF.

Doug Zak claims to this day that the Polygate failures were due to improper=
 fusions.  His catch phrase for this is that they were "cold fusions".  The=
y were proven to be caused by the butt fusion of unlike DRs of extreme diff=
erence.  They were more than one DR difference being DR17 to DR11 and DR15.=
5 to DR11.  No credible and responsible entity in the PE industry will reco=
mmend fusions of more than one DR difference.  Zak and CMF's terminology re=
fers to butt fusion of unlike DR's as "compatible fusion".  Their term is n=
ot a term used by anyone else in the industry for the butt fusion of unlike=
 DR's.

To the untrained eye the fracture surface of a failure due to unlike DR fus=
ions is smooth which can cause a leap to the conclusion that the joint is a=
 cold fusion.  The fracture surface is actually that exhibited by Slow Crac=
k Growth which is a result of the stress concentration at the step change i=
n thickness.

You are to dispute the CMF story on this account when presented with it by =
those in your market.  You will need to frame it as circumstances warrant. =
 If you are not comfortable with this charge you must advise us.

J


